WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.458
Hi! A clock face is round, and a cut sandwich is a triangle. Today we'll learn 2D shapes and shape patterns.

2
00:00:10.608 --> 00:00:15.618
A circle is round. It has no straight sides and no corners.

3
00:00:15.768 --> 00:00:19.530
A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners.

4
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.226
A square has 4 sides, all the same length.

5
00:00:23.376 --> 00:00:30.474
A rectangle has 4 sides; the top and bottom match, and so do the two sides.

6
00:00:30.624 --> 00:00:34.434
Shapes can be sorted by shape, size or colour.

7
00:00:34.584 --> 00:00:40.338
Circle, triangle, circle, triangle, repeating again and again, is a pattern.

8
00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:44.466
Find the part that repeats, then say what comes next.

9
00:00:44.616 --> 00:00:49.098
Fold a circle in half to get a half circle.

10
00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:55.914
Watch out! Things the same size can be different shapes. Look at sides and corners.

11
00:00:56.064 --> 00:00:58.890
Count a triangle's sides: 3.

12
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:05.442
Squares and rectangles both have 4 sides; a square's are all equal.

13
00:01:05.592 --> 00:01:14.514
Your turn! Which shape has 3 sides and 3 corners? Pause and think.

14
00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:19.338
It's a triangle. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:19.488 --> 00:01:27.690
Another one! Which shape has no corners? Pause and think.

16
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.162
A circle has no corners. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:33.312 --> 00:01:42.306
Here's another! Which shape has 4 sides of the same length? Pause and think.

18
00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:46.938
It's a square. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:47.088 --> 00:01:58.146
Try one more! Circle, triangle, circle, triangle, circle. What comes next? Pause and think.

20
00:01:58.296 --> 00:02:03.858
After a circle comes a triangle. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:04.008 --> 00:02:12.042
Try one more! Which shape is a door like? Pause and think.

22
00:02:12.192 --> 00:02:17.514
A door is like a rectangle. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:17.664 --> 00:02:28.002
Try one more! Square, square, circle, repeating. What comes next? Pause and think.

24
00:02:28.152 --> 00:02:35.802
The repeating part is square, square, circle, so next is a square. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:35.952 --> 00:02:44.634
Try one more! How many corners does a triangle have? Pause and think.

26
00:02:44.784 --> 00:02:50.274
A triangle has 3 corners. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:50.424 --> 00:02:58.914
Last one! How many sides does a rectangle have? Pause and think.

28
00:02:59.064 --> 00:03:04.553
A rectangle has 4 sides. Did you get it right?

29
00:03:04.703 --> 00:03:11.465
Remember: count sides and corners to name a shape; for patterns, find the part that repeats.

30
00:03:11.615 --> 00:03:15.233
Find round things at home!

